  "title": "Monthly nomination volume estimates agreed by email, counterparty by counterparty",
  "task_class": "gas_nomination",
  "label_mechanical": "Gas nomination and scheduling: estimate monthly / volume / nomination",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "Ahead of a new flow month, someone in gas logistics needs a per-counterparty, per-point volume figure to nominate. Two patterns show up here. In one, a standing estimate is mailed out as a notice \u2014 \"This is the estimated Josey Ranch nomination for the month of February 2000\" \u2014 repeated the same way for April. In the other, a scheduler asks whether a figure is right (\"Does this average represent a good estimate of the Calpine May nom?\") and colleagues reply with a number and the basis for it: 40,000 for Midcon, 5,000 total as a safe assumption, Southern Union at named points, IFERC 40,000/d totalling 1,240,000. The exchange ends when someone states a number plainly enough to be nominated against; there is no visible system of record in these messages beyond the mail itself.",
    "where_it_stalls": "The figure exists only as prose in someone's reply, so it has to be re-asked rather than looked up. The one waiting signal here is exactly that: a later request reopens a volume already handled once \u2014 \"I want to confirm the May MidCon volumes for Mobil - I think it is 30,000 mmbtu/day?\" \u2014 with the sender guessing the number and asking a person to confirm it. Answers are stated as assumptions (\"I would assume\", \"a safe assumption\") rather than as figures pulled from a source, so nothing in the thread shows where the estimate came from or who owns it.",
    "why_it_recurs": "Nominations are set per counterparty for each new flow month, so the same set of volume questions comes round again every month for the same points and parties.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A single per-counterparty monthly estimate sheet, seeded from the prior month's scheduled volumes and circulated for confirmation before the month starts, would replace the ad-hoc \"is this still 40,000?\" mails and give one place to look the number up afterwards.",
    "coherence": "mixed"
  },
